tus="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HARAGUCHI, TATSUO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHISHITA, KUNIHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKURADA, MUNEO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ZEXEL CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HARAGUCHI TATSUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHISHITA KUNIHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKURADA MUNEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HARAGUCHI, TATSUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHISHITA, KUNIHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKURADA, MUNEO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An air conditioner for vehicle capable of preventing an outdoor heat exchanger of a heat pump air conditioner from frosting and improving heating function by the effective use of heat from engine coolant, comprising a judgment means to judge whether or not the outdoor heat exchanger (5) is under the environment capable of being frosted and a control means to circulate the engine coolant to a radiator (9) when the outdoor heat exchanger (5) is judged by the judgment means to be in the environment capable of being frosted, the outdoor heat exchanger (5) and the radiator (9) comprising heat exchanging parts formed with corrugated fins and a plurality of tubes laminated alternately with these fins and a header communicating with the plurality of tubes and each of the heat exchanging parts being opposed to each other and the fins being formed integrally by common members.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un conditionneur d'air pour véhicules permettant d'éviter que l'échangeur de chaleur extérieur d'un conditionneur d'air à pompe à chaleur ne gèle et permettant d'améliorer la fonction de chauffage par une utilisation efficace de la chaleur provenant du liquide de refroidissement du moteur. Ce conditionneur comprend un moyen d'évaluation permettant d'estimer si l'échangeur de chaleur (5) extérieur est placé ou non dans un environnement susceptible de geler. Ce conditionneur comporte, en outre, un moyen de commande pour assurer la circulation du liquide de refroidissement du moteur jusqu'à un radiateur (9) lorsque l'échangeur de chaleur (5) extérieur est considéré comme susceptible de geler par le moyen d'évaluation. L'échangeur de chaleur extérieur (5) et le radiateur (9) comprennent des éléments d'échange thermique pourvus d'ailettes ondulées et de plusieurs tubes disposés alternativement en couches avec ces ailettes. Un collecteur communique avec les tubes. Les éléments d'échange thermique sont situés en regard les uns des autres, et les ailettes sont formées d'un seul tenant avec des éléments communs.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>